        "text": "Many games even have a pay to win model where players have to spend more money to buy exclusive in game content or in game resources so that they can get an edge in the game. In traditional games, players can earn in game currency and collect digital assets, but these items can't or aren't supposed to be traded outside of the game. In most cases, they don't carry any value beyond the scope of the game. Even when they do, players are often prohibited from monetizing or trading their assets in the real world. The gaming company usually controls and holds the in game assets. Despite the innovative game economy in gamefi, keep in mind that things differ depending on specific gamefi projects. Blockchain technology can and should give players complete control over their in game assets, but that's not always the case. Just because a game is blockchain based.",
